1
00:05:02,307 --> 00:05:08,307
To fight monsters, we created monsters.

2
00:10:04,615 --> 00:10:10,615
Pacific Rim is a action, science fiction, adventure
film directed by Guillermo del Toro.

3
00:15:06,923 --> 00:15:12,923
Using massive piloted robots to combat the alien threat, earth's survivors take the fight
to the invading alien force lurking in the depths of the Pacific Ocean.

4
00:20:09,230 --> 00:20:15,230
Nearly defenseless in the face of the relentless enemy, the forces of mankind have no choice but to turn to
two unlikely heroes who now stand as earth's final hope against the mounting apocalypse.

5
00:25:11,538 --> 00:25:17,538
Raleigh Becket, played by Charlie Hunnam.

6
00:30:13,846 --> 00:30:19,846
Mako Mori, played by Rinko Kikuchi.

7
00:35:16,153 --> 00:35:22,153
Stacker Pentecost, played by Idris Elba.

8
00:40:18,461 --> 00:40:24,461
Herc Hansen, played by Max Martini.

9
00:45:20,769 --> 00:45:26,769
Tendo Choi, played by Clifton Collins Jr..

10
00:50:23,076 --> 00:50:29,076
Hannibal Chau, played by Ron Perlman.

11
00:55:25,384 --> 00:55:31,384
Pacific Rim is a 2013 American monster action film
directed by Guillermo del Toro.

12
01:00:27,692 --> 01:00:33,692
The first film in the Pacific Rim franchise, it stars Charlie Hunnam, Idris Elba, Rinko
Kikuchi, Charlie Day, Robert Kazinsky, Max Martini, and Ron Perlman.

13
01:05:30,000 --> 01:05:36,000
The screenplay was written by Travis Beacham and
del Toro, from a story by Beacham.

14
01:10:32,307 --> 01:10:38,307
The film is set in the future, when Earth is at war with the Kaiju, colossal sea monsters which
have emerged from an interdimensional portal on the bottom of the Pacific Ocean.

15
01:15:34,615 --> 01:15:40,615
To combat the monsters, humanity unites to create the Jaegers, gigantic humanoid mechas,
each controlled by two co-pilots whose minds are joined by a mental link.

16
01:20:36,923 --> 01:20:42,923
Focusing on the war's later days, the story follows Raleigh Becket, a washed-up Jaeger pilot called out of
retirement and teamed with rookie pilot Mako Mori as part of a last-ditch effort to defeat the Kaiju.

17
01:25:39,230 --> 01:25:45,230
Principal photography began on November 14, 2011, in
Toronto and lasted through to April 2012.

18
01:30:41,538 --> 01:30:47,538
The film was produced by Legendary Pictures and distributed by Warner Bros.

19
01:35:43,846 --> 01:35:49,846
It was released on July 12, 2013, in 3D, RealD 3D, IMAX 3D and 4DX, receiving generally positive reviews from critics, who
praised its performances, direction, storyline, action sequences, visual effects, musical score, and nostalgic style.

20
01:40:46,153 --> 01:40:52,153
While it underperformed at the box office in the United States, it was highly
successful in other markets, thus becoming a box office success.

21
01:45:48,461 --> 01:45:54,461
It earned a worldwide total of $411 million—earning $114 million in China alone, its
largest market—becoming Del Toro's most commercially successful film.

22
01:50:50,769 --> 01:50:56,769
The film is regarded as an homage to kaiju, mecha, and anime media.

23
01:55:53,076 --> 01:55:59,076
A sequel titled Pacific Rim Uprising was released on March 23, 2018,
with Universal Pictures as the film's distributor.

24
02:00:55,384 --> 02:01:01,384
The film explores themes of monster, dystopia, giant monster, pacific, alaska.

25
02:05:57,692 --> 02:06:03,692
The tone is thought_provoking.
